    "created_at": "2025-10-02T17:12:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-02T17:12:42Z",
    "body": "I am not sure if we fully solved this issue. Most of the tests pass with these steps, so that's good. However, `/content-security-policy/img-src/icon-blocked.sub.html` still fails with this specification and I think the originally reported flow in #11726 is still relevant. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#create-link-options-from-element now doesn't set a destination. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#create-a-link-request then checks for `null` and bails out.\r\n\r\nWhen I make destination non-nullable and remove `If options's destination is null, then return null.`, then all tests do pass. See https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/39549 for the fixes",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
